// What follows the values of a module once its calls are verified: the ranges of its integers, which decide what can fail
// and must be caught, then ownership (ownership.maxon), which follows the failures to their handlers. The range analysis is
// a later step of the port; until then it accepts what it is given.

// checkRanges is the call site of the range analysis (checked math proofs), for the constants and the functions of a module.
function checkRanges(mutates c Checker, mutates p ast.Project, functions ast.FuncIDList, mutates errs diag.ErrorList)
	_ = 0
end 'checkRanges'
